ok   HTTP/1.1 without a Host header is served: the host is HostAuthorization's to check
ok   serves a bare HttpHandler with no Context or Middleware involved
ok   the bare path's 500 carries the id a RequestId set; a handler without one sends none
ok   the bare path's 500 and 4xx lines carry the request's id; the thread is back on NO_SCOPE after each
ok   a streamed body is written under the request's Scope, the server's stream error line included
ok   an upgraded connection's writer that raises is reported once, with the request's id
ok   a streamed body whose client went away is logged and not reported
ok   an upgraded (101) connection behind RequestId: the id echoed, the writer under the request's Scope, NO_SCOPE after
ok   start raises Cybertrain::PortInUse when the port is already bound
